 (cells markdown newCursorCol)←{leftRight}FormatTable(table cursorRow cursorCol);table2;table3;table4;headerRow;hasColHeaders;dataRows;noOfCols;widths;hasFooter;colHeader;i;col;footerRow;alignment;spaces;noOfLeadingSpaces;currentLine;textLeftOfCursor
⍝ Formats a Markdown table. This function does not know anything about the GUI;
⍝ see `FormatTableInMarkdown` for the function that extracts the table from the
⍝ Markdown and injects the result back into it.
⍝ `⍵` is a three-item vector:
⍝ * `table` is a vector of character vectors: the lines the table consists of, indentation included.
⍝ * `cursorRow` is the index into `table` of the line the cursor is on.
⍝ * `cursorCol` is the number of characters to the left of the cursor on that line.
⍝ If the optional `⍺` is provided, a new column is added. `⍺` must be either "left" or "right".
⍝ The new column is added either to the left or the right of the cursor.
⍝ Returns a three-item vector:
⍝ * `cells` is the formatted table as a matrix of cells, or `⍬` in case `table` is not a table.
⍝ * `markdown` is the formatted table as a vector of character vectors, indentation included.
⍝ * `newCursorCol` is the column the cursor is supposed to be moved to.
 (cells markdown newCursorCol)←⍬ ⍬ ⍬
 :If 0<≢table
     currentLine←cursorRow⊃table                                ⍝ Remember it: `table` is about to be changed
     table2←{' '@(1+⍸'\|'⍷⍵)⊣⍵}¨table                           ⍝ Replace escaped pipes by spaces
     table2←{b←~##.GetMaskForCode ⍵ ⋄ b\b/⍵}¨table2             ⍝ Replace code by spaces
 :AndIf ∧/'|'∊¨table2                                           ⍝ Indeed all are table rows?
     noOfLeadingSpaces←⌊/spaces←+/∧\' '=⊃table
     table←spaces↓¨table
     table←{'|'=↑⍵:⍵ ⋄ '|',⍵}¨table                             ⍝ Add leading pipe where required
     table←##.A.DTB table
     table←{'|'=↑¯1↑⍵:⍵ ⋄ ⍵,'|'}¨table                          ⍝ Add trailing pipe where required
     table←##.TAB ⎕R'    '⊣table                                ⍝ Replace TABs by four spaces
     table2←{' '@(1+⍸'\|'⍷⍵)⊣⍵}¨table                           ⍝ Replace escaped pipes by spaces (again)
     table2←{b←~##.GetMaskForCode ⍵ ⋄ b\b/⍵}¨table2             ⍝ Replace code by spaces (again)
     hasColHeaders←⍬≢headerRow←GetHeaderRow table
     footerRow←''
     :If hasFooter←2<≢table                                     ⍝ Does the table
     :AndIf ~hasFooter←(((footerRow←¯2+≢table2)⊃table)~'| ')∧.='=' ⍝ ... has somewhere ...
         hasFooter←(((footerRow←¯1+≢table2)⊃table)~'| ')∧.='='  ⍝ ... a footer?
     :EndIf
     dataRows←(⍳≢table)~(hasColHeaders/headerRow),(hasFooter/footerRow) ⍝ Pure data rows (without header & footer deviders)
     noOfCols←table2+.=¨'|'                                     ⍝ No of columns in each row
     table,¨←((⌈/noOfCols)-noOfCols)⍴¨'|'                       ⍝ Add column where required
     table←⊃table SplitTableRows table2                         ⍝ Split and reformat
     table←{⍵∧.=' ':⍵ ⋄ ##.A.DLB ⍵}¨table                       ⍝ Remove leading spaces unless a cell is empty
     widths←⌈⌿≢¨table[dataRows;]                                ⍝ Column widths
     :If hasColHeaders
         table[headerRow;]←widths EnlargeColHeader¨table[headerRow;] ⍝ Beef up the column headers but save the colons, if any
     :EndIf
     :If hasFooter
         table[footerRow;]←widths⍴¨'='
     :EndIf
     alignment←⍬
     :For i :In ⍳↑⌽⍴table                                       ⍝ Loop through the columns
         colHeader←↑table[headerRow;i]
         :If ':'∊colHeader                                      ⍝ Did the user define the alignment
             :If '::'≡2⍴¯1⌽colHeader                            ⍝ Centered?
                 table[dataRows;i]←widths[i]{⍵,⍨¨' '⍴⍨¨⌊0.5×⍺-≢¨⍵}##.A.DTB table[dataRows;i]
                 alignment,←'C'
             :ElseIf ':'=¯1↑colHeader                           ⍝ Right-aligned?
                 table[dataRows;i]←↓{⍵⌽⍨-+/∧\' '=⌽⍵}⊃table[dataRows;i]
                 alignment,←'R'
             :Else
                 alignment,←'L'
             :EndIf
         :ElseIf ∧/{0=≢⍵:1 ⋄ ↑↑⎕VFI ⍵}¨headerRow↓table[dataRows;i] ⍝ All cells contain something that is numeric? (ignores col headers & empty cells)
             table[dataRows;i]←↓{⍵⌽⍨-+/∧\' '=⌽⍵}⊃table[dataRows;i]
             alignment,←'R'
         :Else
             alignment,←'L'
         :EndIf
     :EndFor
     table←CompressTable table alignment dataRows hasColHeaders hasFooter headerRow footerRow
     :If 0<⎕NC'leftRight'
         :If 0<≢textLeftOfCursor←##.A.DLB cursorCol↑currentLine
             textLeftOfCursor←{' '@(1+⍸'\|'⍷⍵)⊣⍵}textLeftOfCursor
             textLeftOfCursor←{b←~##.GetMaskForCode ⍵ ⋄ b\b/⍵}textLeftOfCursor
         :EndIf
         :If leftRight≡'left'
             col←0⌈¯1+'|'+.=textLeftOfCursor
         :ElseIf leftRight≡'right'
             col←(1⊃⍴table)⌊'|'+.=textLeftOfCursor
         :EndIf
         table3←((≢table),0)⍴''
         :If col>0
             table3,←col↑[1]table
         :EndIf
         table3,←⊂'    '
         :If (1⊃⍴table)>col
             table3,←col↓[1]table
         :EndIf
         table3[headerRow;col]←⊂'----'
         :If hasFooter
             table3[footerRow;col]←⊂'===='
         :EndIf
     :Else
         table3←table
     :EndIf
     table4←↓'|',(⊃⊃{⍺,'|',⍵}/¨↓⊃¨↓⍉table3),'|'
     cells←table3
     markdown←((≢table4)⍴⊂noOfLeadingSpaces⍴' '),¨table4
     :If 0=⎕NC'leftRight'
         newCursorCol←2
     :Else
         newCursorCol←2++/col≥+\'|'=1⊃table4
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
